    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:clio-ml-engineer:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "24498087307123962f69f6eb25c6dad8c446542388ec4ff42e6aeec568f6e531",
      "output": "About the job\n\nClio is the global leader in legal AI technology, empowering legal professionals and law firms of every size to work smarter, faster, and more securely.\n\nWe are transforming the legal experience for all by bettering the lives of legal professionals while increasing access to justice.\n\nSummary:\n\nWe are currently seeking a Machine Learning Engineer to join our rapidly growing engineering team. This role is for someone who is passionate about building innovative solutions and being exposed to new challenges and technologies while making an impact.\n\nThis role is available to candidates across Canada (excluding Quebec). If you are local to one of our hubs (Burnaby, Calgary, or Toronto) you will be expected to be in office minimum twice per week on one of our Anchor Days.\n\nWhat your team does:\n\nWe at Clio have an amazing team that is on a mission to transform the legal experience for all, and our engineering team’s goal is to deliver an incredible experience to our customers. In the AI team in Clio, we use the latest technology in the space of NLP and GenAI to provide our customers with solutions to make their work more streamlined and efficient allowing them to have more time to focus on their clients’ needs.\n\nA day in the life might look like:\n\n    Develop advanced machine learning models using structured and unstructured data to improve Clio’s customer’s experience\n    Create LLMs based solutions to help Clio’s clients to save time and create efficiencies\n    Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product management, operations and data science to identify new ML-driven features for Clio customers\n    Work in an agile environment with our team of machine learning engineers, MLOps engineering and full stack developers across a variety of projects\n\nWhat you may have:\n\n    Hands-on experience in model development, particularly with traditional machine learning, NLP, and transformer-based models;\n    Proficiency in data manipulation, cleaning, and preprocessing for complex unstructured datasets;\n    Experience with agentic frameworks and workflows \n    Experience working with open-source LLM foundation models and APIs for commercial LLMs, such as ChatGPT or Gemini;\n    A proven ability to quickly learn new technologies and adapt to a dynamic, fast-paced environment with distributed teams and customers;\n    A portfolio of past projects showcasing your successes, challenges, and growth as a machine learning expert;\n    Exceptional communication skills and the ability to build trust with both internal teams and external customers;\n    A strong desire to continuously learn, challenge yourself, and refine your craft as a machine learning engineer.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1061,
        "completion_tokens": 516
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:27:54-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:coca-cola-data-scientist:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "153868931b46d65bb26fbb9c3f18d2a861ab725078e5e5952a486b976b9eb676",
      "output": "Role Details\n\n    Work Location – Toronto\n    Hybrid Environment – This position currently offers a hybrid work schedule. Subject to change. The in-office requirement is a minimum of three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday & Thursday), with the flexibility to work remotely on the remaining days.\n\nAbout This Opportunity\n\nWe are recruiting for a Data Scientist to join our Data Science and Advanced Analytics team. This Advanced Analytics role is part of the broader Technology function and plays a key role in supporting high impact, data driven initiatives across the organization. The team partners with stakeholders in commercial strategy, sales execution, and operations to address complex business challenges through advanced analytics and machine learning.\n\n\nAs a Data Scientist, you will contribute to cross functional projects involving demand modeling, promotion and trade spend optimization, pricing and elasticity analysis, network and inventory optimization, and scenario modeling. You will work closely with business partners to translate exploratory analytical work into scalable, production ready solutions that enhance planning, strengthen decision making, and improve execution across the organization.\n\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to leverage your experience in data science, advanced analytics, or applied machine learning to help solve meaningful business challenges and turn complex data into practical, scalable insights.\nResponsibilities\n\n    Contribute to analytics initiatives using statistical and machine learning techniques to solve business problems in demand forecasting, pricing, and product optimization.\n    Support the development and improvement of analytical models to understand demand drivers and price elasticity, ensuring insights are practical, reliable, and business-relevant.\n    Assist in building tools and analytical processes that improve trade spend effectiveness and promotional performance, enabling smarter commercial and sales decisions.\n    Support analytics initiatives that enhance operational planning and execution, applying data-driven insights as the function expands into operations-focused areas.\n    Create clear visualizations and collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate data insights into actionable recommendations for commercial, sales, and operations stakeholders.\n\nQualifications\n\n    Bachelor’s degree or a college diploma in a quantitative or technical field (e.g., Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Engineering); a Master’s degree is considered an asset.\n    3+ years of experience in data science, advanced analytics, or applied machine learning roles, with exposure to business-focused analytics.\n    Strong experience working with large, complex datasets and proficiency in SQL and Python.\n    Experience applying statistical modeling and machine learning techniques, such as regression-based models, tree-based models and optimization approaches.\n    Foundational understanding of demand forecasting, elasticity modeling, promotional analysis, or scenario modeling.\n    Familiarity with analytics development within Databricks and the Azure data ecosystem is considered an asset.\n    Strong proficiency in data visualization tools such as Power BI (preferred) or Tableau.\n    Ability to communicate analytical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n    Proactive mindset with the ability to work through ambiguity, take initiative, and suggest new analytical approaches or opportunities to improve business outcomes.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1453,
        "completion_tokens": 582
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:28:39-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:dayforce-product-ai-intern:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "37770a9a1ef03c1c857404b657e9c233757406d3ff265cf926ed7e491bcc3214",
      "output": "Dayforce, a global leader in Human Capital Management (HCM) with headquarters in Toronto, Ontario, and Minneapolis, Minnesota, operates across North America, EMEA, and APJ regions. Our Cloud HCM platform, recognized for its unified database and continuous calculation engine, enhances efficiency, productivity, and compliance for global workforces. We are committed to \"Making Work Life Better™\" for employees, customers, and partners worldwide.\n\nAs an Intern at Dayforce, you’ll gain real-world experience with meaningful responsibilities, access to development programs, and the chance to collaborate globally, bringing new ideas and optimizing processes across multiple business units.\n\nJob Title: Product & AI Intern\n\nLocation: Virtual\n\nDuration: Fall 2026 – 4 months (September 2026 – December 2026)\n\nAvailability: *Full-time availability of 37.5 – 40 hours weekly is required to be eligible for this opportunity.\n\nWe are seeking a technical AI Product Intern to support our GenAI and AI Agent product initiatives. In this role, you will work directly with the AI product team to develop prototypes that spark future product innovation, as well as help improve model performance, evaluate multilingual model output quality. Furthermore, you will have the opportunity to help us evolve our product analytics capabilities in Pendo, and craft meaningful content in Confluence. This internship is ideal for a Computer Science or Engineering student with a passion for machine learning, AI, experimentation, and turning messy problems into working solutions.\n\nWhat You’ll Get To Do\n\nBuild working demos in live code to communicate product opportunities\nCreate annotated datasets to improve our LLM-based systems\nAssist with hands-on evaluation of multilingual model output\nDevelop and refine product analytics in Pendo and analyze product usage data in Pendo and Databricks to generate insights that inform our roadmap\nCraft and refine meaningful content and documentation (e.g. Confluence) for broad stakeholder communications\nSupport our teams’ development workflows and experimentation infrastructure\n\nSkills And Experience We Value\n\nProven experience with machine learning, preferably GenAI or LLM applications\nExperience with programming languages: Python and SQL, etc.\nComfort with tools such as (or similar to): Databricks, Pendo, Visual Studio, etc.\nEntrepreneurial mindset: works with minimal guidance and solves their own problems\nAbility to translate ambiguous tasks into clear outputs\nStrong communication skills and curiosity about how product and ML intersect\n\nWhat Would Really Make You Stand Out\n\nFront-end experience (React, Streamlit, etc.) for prototyping\nFamiliarity with multilingual NLP or localization tools\nThis internship is a chance to work on frontier tech with real-world applications and visibility. You’ll get to experiment, deliver, and influence the future of AI at Dayforce.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 995,
        "completion_tokens": 580
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:29:38-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:deloitte-ai-ml-models-consultant-analyst:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "499f159583da09604791015bb701ead05cb296cf26baed2670cdbe1d09b88e90",
      "output": "Analyst/Consultant, AI/ML Models - Financial Engineering & Modeling (Permanent / Contract)\n\nJob Type: PermanentWork Model: HybridReference code: 133514Primary Location: Toronto, ONAll Available Locations: Toronto, ON\n\nWhat will your typical day look like?\n\nIn this role you will help financial services industry (FSI) clients face quantitative issues with informed confidence. Using your deep technical skills and leveraging our global network of experts, you’ll provide professional advice to our FSI clients in a wide range of situations. The result? Our clients will be better placed to take control and receive the best solutions to their complex challenges.\n\nDevelop/validate/review Large Language Models models (LLMs) based on industry best practices.\n\nYou will also be able to learn and work in other quantitative and analytical areas such as credit modeling, forecasting and stress testing and customer behavior modeling.\n\nAbout The Team\n\nDeloitte’s Risk, Regulatory & Forensics practice delivers highly specialized advisory solutions for companies facing critical business events where significant value is at stake, in every phase of the economic cycle.\n\nOur work is often high profile, high impact, and highly rewarding. If you’re looking for a challenge and an opportunity to grow your career alongside the best and brightest in the industry, you’ll find it in Risk, Regulatory & Forensics at Deloitte. Broaden your skills. Broaden your reach. Broaden your career. It’s all possible at Deloitte.\n\nYou are someone with:\n\nRelevant experience in AI/ML domain\nKnowledge of NLP, LLMs (extractive and generative), fine-tuning, development, and deployment of LLM model. Familiar with higher level trends in LLMs and open-source platforms\nCreatively solution new features for the clients’ Generative AI offerings, including testing, evaluating and benchmarking different LLMs and toolchains\nExperience with Langchain and RAG\nDemonstrated hands-on experience with Python, Hugging Face, TensorFlow, Keras, PyTorch or similar statistical tools\nSolid academic background with a PhD or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or related field\nExceptional problem-solving abilities, meticulous attention to detail and a talent for logical reason\nCuriosity and enthusiasm about new and unfamiliar technologies with ability to learn technical/scientific concepts quickly with minimal direction",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1279,
        "completion_tokens": 498
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:30:22-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:ebay-applied-researcher-1:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "7fb7207733b2bf04f058e6b92140a485b7366be652e5a44885ca7484fb3234df",
      "output": "At eBay, we're more than a global ecommerce leader — we’re changing the way the world shops and sells. Our platform empowers millions of buyers and sellers in more than 190 markets around the world. We’re committed to pushing boundaries and leaving our mark as we reinvent the future of ecommerce for enthusiasts.\n\nOur customers are our compass, authenticity thrives, bold ideas are welcome, and everyone can bring their unique selves to work — every day. We're in this together, sustaining the future of our customers, our company, and our planet.\n\nJoin a team of passionate thinkers, innovators, and dreamers — and help us connect people who help connect people and build communities to create economic opportunity for all.\n\nThe Search Ranking and Monetization team sits at the core of eBay’s marketplace, powering the search and advertising experiences that connect millions of buyers and sellers every day. As the largest contributor to eBay’s advertising program, the team focuses on redefining e-commerce advertising through cutting-edge machine learning, large-scale experimentation, and a strong focus on customer value.\n\nWe are looking for applied researchers who are excited by the scale and complexity of online advertising and search. In this role, you will design and deploy advanced models that shape how listings are ranked, how ads are served, and how buyers discover the inventory they love. You will work closely with partner teams across product, engineering, and analytics, and you will have opportunities to share your work internally and in external forums and conferences.\n\nWhat You Will Accomplish\n    Deliver scientifically robust solutions that improve key buyer and seller outcomes, such as relevance, engagement, and marketplace efficiency.\n    Design, build, and iterate on machine learning models and data pipelines that power ranking, recommendation, and advertising products in eBay search.\n    Partner with cross-functional teams to define problem statements, validate hypotheses, and translate research into scalable, production-ready solutions.\n    Promote and standardize scientific methodologies, experimentation practices, and best-in-class evaluation frameworks across the organization.\n    Share technical and research contributions through internal forums and external conferences, helping position eBay as a leader in e-commerce advertising.\n    Continuously expand your expertise in large-scale machine learning, big data technologies, and online experimentation while mentoring and learning from peers.\n\nWhat You Will Bring\n    MS or PhD in Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent practical experience.\n    1–3 years of relevant industry experience with a PhD, or 3–5 years with an MS, working in areas such as online advertising, ranking, recommendation, targeting, fraud detection, or related fields.\n    Hands-on experience applying machine learning techniques (e.g., classification, regression, ranking, recommendation) in large-scale, real-world systems.\n    Proficiency with big data tools and technologies such as Hadoop, SQL, and Spark, and comfort working with large, complex datasets.\n    Strong programming skills in Python or R, and in at least one of Java, Scala, or C/C++, with a focus on building production-quality solutions.\n    A track record of scientific impact demonstrated by 2 or more related publications in reputable conferences or journals, and the ability to clearly communicate research findings to both technical and non-technical audiences.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1007,
        "completion_tokens": 672
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:31:26-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:fgf-brands-ai-engineer-new-grad:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "49f337d136580e40e370b4b2b7aec25a895d0586006ff30dc52b9c1d6c27fac0",
      "output": "About the job\n\nSummary\n\nFGF Brands is on a mission to lead the food manufacturing industry through innovation, speed, and smart execution. As we enter the next phase of our Digital and AI transformation, we are creating a unique, high-impact role designed for a curious, tech-savvy, business-minded young graduate who wants to be at the intersection of technology, executive leadership, and industry reinvention.\n\nWe’re hiring an AI Engineer who builds with AI. This is not a passive “learn AI on the job” role. It’s for someone who has prototypes, ships, and experiments—turning real operational problems into working software. You’ll work directly with senior leaders across supply chain and operations, building agentic AI tools that solve real business problems and get used in production.\n\nPrimary Responsibilities\n\nBuild and ship AI-powered and agentic solutions focused on supply chain and operations\nRapidly prototype and iterate—POCs in days, not quarters\nApply LLMs to real-world data using RAG, fine-tuning, and agent frameworks\nBuild internal tools, automations, and dashboards that drive measurable impact\nPartner with senior leaders to translate business friction into working software\nEvaluate and integrate emerging AI tools and frameworks\nClearly explain what you build through demos and practical walkthroughs\n\nRequired Experience\n\nA recent graduate (0–3 years of experience)\nBackground in Computer Science, Mathematics, Engineering, or a related technical field\nYou’ve built real AI projects and can show them (side projects count)\nStrong Python, APIs, version control, and basic system design\nHands-on experience with LLMs (prompting, RAG, fine-tuning, or agentic frameworks)\nAble to explain technical concepts simply to non-technical partners",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 768,
        "completion_tokens": 361
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:32:02-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:hellofresh-ml-engineer-operations-technology:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "9860db281317c65736fce2c83a971b09bbb65a0f9393f6708c28fc20323efc9d",
      "output": "We are hiring a Machine Learning Engineer in our ML Solutions squad to help build innovative generative AI products that provide AI-powered assistants to HelloFresh's culinary Chefs helping them editorialize content, validate recipe data, detect issues, suggest corrections, and ideate. As a Machine Learning Engineer, you will primarily contribute to our agentic generative AI system that automates recipe content production, while also supporting the MLOps platform that enables data scientists across the company to develop, deploy, and monitor ML models at scale.\n\nDevelop and maintain an agentic GenAI system that integrates with HelloFresh's culinary content pipeline (API development, LLM orchestration, image generation).\nDesign and implement production-grade AI Agent evaluations to measure quality, reliability, and performance of generative outputs.\nDesign and build scalable, production-grade ML systems capable of handling large datasets, complex model pipelines, and real-time API integrations.\nContribute to our MLOps platform — a set of tools and services built on Databricks, MLFlow, and Prefect that help data scientists develop, deploy, and maintain ML applications.\nCollaborate with data scientists, product managers, and culinary stakeholders to translate business needs into reliable AI & ML products.\nImprove operational excellence through automation, monitoring, drift detection, and data quality practices.\nStay up-to-date on advancements in generative AI, agentic workflows, and MLOps tooling, and propose improvements to the team's development lifecycle.\nAll other duties, as assigned\n\nStrong software development skills in Python and SQL, including DevOps practices, test-driven development (TDD), spec-driven development, and fluency working with AI coding agents.\nHands-on experience building and maintaining production ML systems, including model serving, monitoring, and CI/CD pipelines.\nFamiliarity or interest in generative AI (LLMs, image generation, prompt engineering, agentic architectures).\nExperience with modern MLOps tooling such as MLFlow, feature engineering, Kubernetes, and workflow orchestration (e.g., Prefect). Experience with PySpark and Databricks is a plus.\nA passion for building developer tools and platforms that improve productivity and enable other teams to scale ML adoption.\nAbility to communicate complex technical findings to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n\nFlexible Hybrid work. Flexible Hybrid is a people-first approach that is based on choice, trust, personalization, and empowers teams to choose when and how often they work from the office and work from home, in addition to team days and company days. This means a minimum of 2 days in office per week, with most teams in office between 2-3 days a week.\n\nHelloFresh Canada uses AI-integrated technology to help us process and evaluate applications more efficiently. This includes tools that screen and assess candidate qualifications based on the requirements for this role. While these tools assist our workflow, all final selection decisions are made by our hiring team.\n\nThis is a posting for an existing vacancy. We are actively seeking to fill this position.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1329,
        "completion_tokens": 617
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:32:58-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:huawei-ai-ml-researcher:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "7913d744ffbb79fd4c3702730850ae23821dd1da61effc67165646850f6c6ea1",
      "output": "Huawei Canada has an immediate permanent opening for a Researcher.\n\nThe Huawei Human-Machine Interaction Lab unites global researchers, engineers, and designers to redefine human technology relationships through user centered, hands on research. We focus on agentic AI and multimodal interaction (voice, touch, vision, gesture) across smartphones, wearables, and emerging devices—advancing agentic workflows, multi-agent orchestration, and intuitive human-AI interfaces. By tightly integrating sensing, algorithms, and systems, our prototype driven work ships directly to products, enabling seamless task delegation and human AI collaboration at scale.\n\nBuild and ship AI/ML capabilities that power next-generation Huawei intelligent products, including smartphones, smart glasses, wearables, and emerging devices.\nDesign, prototype, and evaluate deep learning models across vision, language, audio, and video, and advance their integration into real product experiences.\nTranslate cutting-edge research in generative AI, foundation models, and efficient inference into robust, scalable prototypes and product-ready solutions.\nOwn end-to-end model development workflows: data curation, training, fine-tuning, evaluation, optimization, and deployment on device or in the cloud.\nPartner with researchers, engineers, designers, and product managers to identify high-impact opportunities and deliver measurable user and business outcomes.\nContribute to a culture of technical excellence through reproducible experiments, thorough documentation, code review, and knowledge sharing.\nPublish and patent innovations at top-tier venues when appropriate.\n\nPhD, Master’s, or Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Statistics, Mathematics, or a related field.\nSolid foundation in machine learning, deep learning, and statistical modeling; hands-on experience building and training models with PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX, or similar frameworks.\nTrack record of translating research ideas into working prototypes, demonstrable systems, or shipped product features.\nExperience with one or more of: computer vision, natural language processing, speech/audio processing, generative models, multimodal learning, recommendation systems, or efficient model optimization.\nStrong software engineering skills in Python; familiarity with C++, CUDA, or on-device inference frameworks is an asset.\nComfortable working with large-scale datasets, distributed training, model evaluation, and MLOps tooling.\nExcellent problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills in cross-functional, fast-moving environments.\nResearch contributions via publications, patents, or open-source projects are an asset.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 931,
        "completion_tokens": 498
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:33:42-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:industrial-and-commercial-bank-of-china-data-science-analyst:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "5df48a575ace86e6fe45f40403906e62ebeb13aa3c0e9cdf270926b99d81465f",
      "output": "Job Title: Data Science Analyst\n\nReporting to: Head of Information Technology Department\n\nJob Description and Responsibilities:\n    Develop program using Python, Oracle Procedure, Java and other tools for analytical data mining, software development, or business reporting.\n    Responsible for project co-ordination related to the development and management of all project-related development, participate and manage in the design, specifications, coding, testing and implementation of bank’s application program and business reporting.\n    Lead and facilitate sessions with business units to gather requirements, refine and document use cases, business rules, scenarios, and data, as well as functional systems requirements throughout the development lifecycle.\n    Investigate and resolve application-related problems.\n    Provide second-level support for the bank’s application system, including after-hour support as required.\n\nQualifications:\n    Undergraduate degree in Computer Science and Data Science related fields;\n    Be familiar with Python, SQL, BI report tools and Java;\n    Good working knowledge of project management ;\n    Excellent customer service skills;\n    Able to communicate and writing skills in English and Mandarin or Cantonese;\n    Ability to set priorities and work efficiently under pressure of high volume;\n    Must be an independent problem solver with troubleshooting, decision making and analytical skills.\n\nWork Location: In person",
