    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:motion-recruitment-ml-engineer:nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b": {
      "input_hash": "448a55d4c0bb73932102c6791ca4e1ca0214483a52939821e269f19a5087a81f",
      "output": "About the job\n\nAn exciting opportunity based in Toronto, Canada (hybrid), with a fast-growing, product-driven company building innovative financial technology solutions. This full time role focuses on designing and scaling modern machine learning systems using technologies such as Python, PyTorch, Scikit-learn, and cloud platforms.\n\nThis is a unique chance to join a high-growth team at a pivotal stage - where product-market fit is established and innovation is accelerating. The company is looking for someone who thrives on building impactful ML solutions end-to-end and enjoys working in a fast-paced environment. If you're passionate about deploying scalable AI systems, optimizing perfor,ance, and influencing criticical production decisions - this role is for you.\n\nRequired Skills & Experience\n\n    Strong experience in Python \n    Experience with machine learning libraries (Scikit-learn, LightGBM, PyTorch) \n    Hands-on experience with data manipulation tools (Pandas, NumPy) and SQL/NoSQL databases \n    Familiarity with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure) \n    Knowledge of MLOps practices, including CI/CD pipelines \n\nDesired Skills & Experience\n\n    Experience with MLOps tools such as MLflow, Kubeflow, or SageMaker \n    Familiarity with containerization and orchestration tools (Docker, Kubernetes) \n    Experience building and deploying machine learning models in production \n\nWhat You Will Be Doing\n\nTech Breakdown\n\n    50% Machine Learning Model Development \n    25% Data Engineering & Pipeline Development \n    15% MLOps & Deployment \n    10% Collaboration & Strategy \n\nDaily Responsibilities\n\n    65% Hands On \n    10% Management Duties \n    25% Team Collaboration",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 702,
        "completion_tokens": 380
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:39:00-0400"
