    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:cibc-quantitative-analyst:google/gemma-3-4b-it": {
      "input_hash": "374af077409c6d3ee8a0856a0d369339dfc5cd681f2e7e11378cfbe71297b66e",
      "output": "\n\nThe Quantitative Research Team at CIBC Global Asset Management is responsible for developing and managing systematic investment strategies across equities and fixed income, as well as improving the investment process of discretionary mandates. As a Quantitative Research Analyst, you'll contribute to the research and development of systematic active equity strategies with an AUM of over $11 Billion. You'll support the design and implementation of quantitative models, conduct empirical research, and help translate investment ideas into actionable insights. Working alongside portfolio managers and senior researchers, you'll play an important role in advancing alpha research and portfolio construction methodologies.\n\nAt CIBC we enable the work environment most optimal for you to thrive in your role. To successfully perform the work, you'll be on-site full-time.\n\nThe expected annualized base salary range for this role is $100,000 to $170,000.\n\nIn addition to base pay, compensation for this role includes participation in an annual discretionary incentive or bonus program.\n\nThe following responsibilities are expected:\n\n*   Quantitative Research & Modelling – Contribute to the development and validation of quantitative models, including factor models and portfolio construction frameworks, to support systematic investment strategies.\n*   Data Analysis & Insights – Analyze large datasets to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and generate actionable investment insights that support the team's research agenda.\n*   Research Support – Collaborate with portfolio managers and senior researchers to translate investment ideas into well-documented, production-ready analytics and research findings.\n*   Technology & Tools – Support the development and maintenance of analytical tools and codebases, primarily using Python and SQL, to enhance research workflows and investment processes.\n*   Communication – Present research findings and analytical results clearly to diverse audiences, including Analysts, Portfolio Managers, and IT professionals, with varying levels of technical expertise.\n\nYou will succeed if you:\n\n*   Contribute to the development and validation of quantitative models, including factor models and portfolio construction frameworks, to support systematic investment strategies.\n*   Analyze large datasets to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and generate actionable investment insights.\n*   Collaborate with portfolio managers and senior researchers to translate investment ideas into well-documented, production-ready analytics and research findings.\n*   Support the development and maintenance of analytical tools and codebases, primarily using Python and SQL.\n*   Present research findings and analytical results clearly to diverse audiences.\n\nYou are motivated by collective success. You know that teamwork can transform a good idea into a great one. You know that an inclusive team that enjoys working together can bring a vision to life. You give meaning to data. You enjoy investigating complex problems and making sense of information. You communicate detailed information in a meaningful way. You love to learn. You're passionate about growing your knowledge. You have a strong sense of curiosity. You're passionate about financial markets and investing. You have a genuine interest in how markets work and are driven by the opportunity to apply quantitative methods to real-world investment challenges.\n\nYou can demonstrate experience in Python (required) and SQL (preferred), including strong knowledge of machine learning libraries (e.g., scikit-learn, PyTorch, or TensorFlow). It’s an asset if you have familiarity with quantitative research tools and financial data platforms. You have a degree in a STEM field (Computer Science/Engineering, Physics, Mathematics, Statistics, or a related discipline). A graduate degree (Master’s or PhD) is preferred.\n\nJob Location\nToronto-141 Bay, 18th Floor\n\nEmployment Type\nRegular\n\nWeekly Hours\n37.5\n\nSkills\nAnalytical Thinking, Decision Making, Machine Learning (ML), Professional Presentation, Python (Programming Language), Quantitative Financial Analysis, Quantitative Models, Researching, Research Reporting",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1664,
        "completion_tokens": 770
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:56:35-0400"
