    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:td-applied-ml-scientist-graduate:google/gemma-3-4b-it": {
      "input_hash": "9c7dbb97e2ed6047bdce6966e8df8fedcb952ba60480a1d7ac39388ed6928038",
      "output": "\n\nThe Applied Machine Learning Scientist will perform a variety of activities, which may include:\n\n*   Apply advanced machine learning methods to conduct data-driven research, identify opportunities, and make tangible recommendations to senior management.\n*   Collaborate with business partners to identify opportunities for process optimization and informed decision-making and build innovative solutions.\n*   Work with structured and unstructured data and prepare data sets for machine learning through integration, cleaning, feature engineering, scaling and transforming data\n*   Build production-scale solutions and work with deployment teams to integrate in business operations\n*   Leverage visualization methods to represent results and communicate outcomes to technical and non-technical audiences\n\nJob Requirements:\n\n*   Must be graduated between May 2025 and December 2026 with a Graduate degree in Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, and/or Data Analytics or related.\n*   Strong statistical and analytical skills as well as a passion for analytics are necessary.\n*   Experience with analyzing large data sets, drawing insights and inferences, and communicating outputs.\n*   Experienced in one or more of:\n    *   Big Data – Programming, Data/Text Mining, Optimization, Algorithm Development, Automation, Data Visualization, Simulation\n    *   Machine Learning – Predictive Analytics, Regression, Logit Modeling, Model development, Discrete Choice, Propensity Modeling, Natural Language Processing, Generative AI.\n    *   Software Engineering – Code Quality, Version Control, Object-Oriented Programming\n*   Strong technical knowledge and experience with one or more of: Python, R, Spark, SQL, SAS, Java, or C/C++\n*   Technical knowledge or experience with Cloud environments as well as experience with Data Management, and Project Management are a plus.\n*   Must have strong leadership qualities including demonstrating initiative, establishing priorities and using strong communication, analytical and problem-solving skills to add value to each initiative, project or team assigned to.\n*   Able to participate as part of a team with targeted deliverables, working on initiatives designed to improve decisions, processes, systems, and applications which support our key businesses.\n*   Remain current with emerging trends and technologies in Data Science\n\nThe Applied Machine Learning Scientist is part of the Analytics Insights & AI team. This team provides in-depth experience, complemented by programming, coaching, tools and support. The role is part of an 18-month rotational program (two nine-month rotations) to gain exposure and experience to opportunities within the Analytics Insights & AI team. Associates have access to programming, tools and a community of support for their pursuits and interests beyond the 9-5, including leadership talks, lunch and learns, self-development workshops, TD sponsored conferences, socials, team challenges, volunteer opportunities, career coaching and more. This role is part of a cohort along with other TD Associates from across Canada.\n\nThe role’s mission is to apply advanced machine learning methods to conduct data-driven research, identify opportunities, and make tangible recommendations to senior management. The scope of the role is to collaborate with business partners to identify opportunities for process optimization and informed decision-making and build innovative solutions. The organizational impact is to improve decisions, processes, systems, and applications which support our key businesses.\n\nApplication Deadline: September 25th 2026\nAnticipated Start Date: January 4th, 2027 (pending academic completion) \nApplications must include a transcript, cover letter (one letter-sized page or less) and a resume (maximum of 2 pages).",
