    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:cerebras-ml-performance-benchmarking-engineer:google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite": {
      "input_hash": "6aaed90932faa76a53d70c368c4baf97bdc9ec5e59f63370c83aeff34ba72072",
      "output": "About the job\n\nCerebras Systems builds the world's largest AI chip, 56 times larger than GPUs. This architecture allows Cerebras to deliver industry-leading training and inference speeds; over 10 times faster than GPU-based hyperscale cloud inference services.\n\nThis order of magnitude increase in speed is transforming the user experience of AI applications, unlocking real-time iteration and increasing intelligence via additional agentic computation.\n\nCerebras works with the leading model labs, global enterprises, and cutting-edge AI-native startups. OpenAI recently announced a multi-year partnership with Cerebras, to deploy 750 megawatts of scale, transforming key workloads with ultra high-speed inference.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nThe Inference Core Platform group is at the heart of Cerebras' mission to deliver the world’s fastest AI inference. Our team builds the foundational software and hardware infrastructure that powers low-latency, high-speed, high-throughput deployment on the Cerebras Wafer-Scale Engine (WSE). We are responsible for the full stack—from model compilation and scheduling down to custom hardware kernels and driver development.\n\nThe ML Performance Benchmarking team plays a pivotal role in shaping the performance and scalability of AI inference on one of the most advanced computing systems ever built. We drive the bring-up of core inference capabilities and deliver performance improvements at every stage of development – from early prototyping to production deployment.\n\nWe're looking for passionate engineers to join us in redefining the limits of AI inference. If you thrive on building systems that measure, analyze, and optimize performance at scale, this is your opportunity to make a transformative impact on the future of AI.\n\nScope Of The Team Includes\n\n    Core Inference Observability – Design and implement end-to-end telemetry systems across the software stack, providing deep visibility into inference performance and enabling rapid iteration before and after deployment.\n    Benchmarking Infrastructure – Architect, build, and scale the automation that generates, analyzes, and visualizes performance data used to inform business decisions across engineering and leadership.\n    Performance Analysis – Dive deep into system behavior, dissect performance bottlenecks, and deliver actionable insights that directly influence which features ship and how they evolve.\n    Feature Integration – Partner closely with Core Platform teams to define rigorous testing methodologies that validate inference features for peak performance.\n\nSkills & Qualifications\n\n    Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Engineering, Systems Engineering, or a related field.\n    Proficiency in Python and/or C++ programming.\n    Proven experience in building and scaling automated infrastructure.\n    Strong background in throughput and performance optimization techniques, especially in complex, large-scale systems.\n    Excellent problem-solving skills and a strong analytical mindset.\n    Demonstrated ability to dive deep into new domains.\n    Ability to work in a fast-paced, ambiguous, and collaborative environment.\n\nPreferred Skills & Qualifications\n\n    Familiarity with problem-solving at the intersection of hardware and software.\n    Hands-on experience with AI workloads and architectures is a plus.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1047,
        "completion_tokens": 618
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:58:55-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:cibc-analyst-global-investment-banking:google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite": {
      "input_hash": "2848dc50c2e0b0e94d90f82dbc9015a8aeaf06ebf1637e9e1f9f70ef06b6bc27",
      "output": "What You’ll Be Doing \n\nCIBC Capital Markets provides corporate, government, and institutional clients with innovative solutions to help them raise capital, and grow and invest actively throughout North America, Latin America, and key financial centres around the world. Our mission is to bring Canadian Capital Markets products to Canada and the rest of the world, and also bring the world to Canada.\n \n\nCIBC Capital Markets Mergers & Acquisitions group of professionals are dedicated specifically to advising clients on mergers, acquisitions, joint ventures, hostile takeovers, buyouts, takeover defense and restructurings.  There is an extensive amount of interaction with other groups within the firm in order to provide clients with customized financing and advisory solutions. \n\nAs part of the M&A group, you will be expected to provide a broad range of analytical, research and presentation preparation support to all the professionals as well as gaining exposure to working with individuals from various groups across the firm. A team approach to executing coverage and financing assignments is designed to provide progressive, on-the-job training. The role of an Analyst within CIBC’s Mergers & Acquisitions (M&A) Investment Banking group is challenging and fast-paced.  It requires dedication, a passion for excellence, and an exceptional work ethic.\n \n\nThe role of an Analyst within CIBC’s Mergers & Acquisitions (M&A) Investment Banking group is challenging and fast-paced.  It requires dedication, a passion for excellence, and an exceptional work ethic.\n \n\nHow You’ll Succeed\n\n    Client Proposals - Assist in analyzing and developing proposals for mergers, asset or company divestitures or acquisitions, and other financial products and advisory services\n    Transaction Execution – Take an active role in day-to-day transaction execution across sell-side, buy-side, fairness opinions, and other assignments\n    Financial Modeling - Develop and audit sophisticated financial models\n    Collaboration - Participate in cross-functional teams and liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in executing mandates or preparing proposals for clients\n    Research - Prepare industry and financial analysis to determine client recommendations\n    Analysis - Lead industry comparables and precedent transaction analyses\n    Due Diligence - Assist in company due diligence investigations\n    Marketing Materials - Prepare confidential offering memoranda and other marketing materials\n    Relationship Building - Take advantage of in-depth technical and industry knowledge, as well as the geopolitical environment to generate ideas/opportunities that can be discussed with the relevant relationship manager and/or deal/coverage team. Coordinate client-focused and/or deal-focused “brainstorming” sessions with relevant team members and product specialists. Liaise with other units of CIBC Capital Markets in preparing proposals for clients. Develop relationships and actively communicate with various appropriate contacts at the client. Develop and maintain an internal network with product groups, other business groups, etc. Develop and maintain an external network with the market (i.e. key stakeholders, prospects, etc.) and support CIBC’s image through involvement in community activities.\n\n                       \n\nWho You Are\n\n    Previous Investment Banking or M&A transaction advisory experience required. Detailed, professional-level knowledge of Canadian M&A processes across different mandate types (sell-side, buy-side, etc.) is considered an asset.\n    You have completed an undergraduate degree in Finance or Engineering. Completion of a CPA or CFA, is beneficial.\n    You know that details matter.  Extremely dedicated and motivated individual with high career aspirations. Must be capable of assuming high levels of responsibility within short time frames.  Ability to work well under pressure with multiple or competing deadlines while maintaining meticulous attention to detail. Must be able to accept flexibility in required personal time commitments to complete work assignments.\n    You can demonstrate technical skills (Programs, Methodologies, Systems). Excellent analytical abilities, including demonstrated knowledge of valuation techniques and practices. Knowledge of accounting principles relating to financial statement preparation and business combinations. Strong technical skills as it relates to Microsoft Office applications (Excel, Word, PowerPoint), industry technology (Bloomberg, Factset) and applicable software.\n    You have advanced internal and client-focused communication skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills are important to ensuring smooth transaction execution and timely delivery of materials. Ability to comfortably liaise with equivalent professionals on the client side is considered a strong asset.\n    You’re motivated by collective success. Well-developed interpersonal and relationship-building skills in order to develop, manage and leverage relationships with clients, and internal and/or external business partners. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills sufficient to provide detailed explanation and interpretation of factual and conceptual information and ideas related to complex technical and conceptual issues. Unquestioned professionalism, ethics and reputation and proven ability to exercise strong independent judgment when making business decisions and/or representing CIBC Capital Markets.\n\nSkills\nAnalytical Thinking, Capital Markets, Financial Markets Analysis, Investment Banking, Investment Valuation, Mergers and Acquisitions (M&A), Research Analysis, Wealth Management, Work Collaboratively",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1986,
        "completion_tokens": 1013
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:58:59-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:cibc-quantitative-analyst:google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite": {
      "input_hash": "374af077409c6d3ee8a0856a0d369339dfc5cd681f2e7e11378cfbe71297b66e",
      "output": "Quantitative Analyst/Senior Quantitative Analyst\n\nWhat you'll be doing\n\nThe Quantitative Research Team at CIBC Global Asset Management is responsible for developing and managing systematic investment strategies across equities and fixed income, as well as improving the investment process of discretionary mandates. As a Quantitative Research Analyst, you'll contribute to the research and development of systematic active equity strategies with an AUM of over $11 Billion. You'll support the design and implementation of quantitative models, conduct empirical research, and help translate investment ideas into actionable insights. Working alongside portfolio managers and senior researchers, you'll play an important role in advancing alpha research and portfolio construction methodologies.\n\nHow you'll succeed\n\nQuantitative Research & Modelling – Contribute to the development and validation of quantitative models, including factor models and portfolio construction frameworks, to support systematic investment strategies.\nData Analysis & Insights – Analyze large datasets to identify patterns, test hypotheses, and generate actionable investment insights that support the team's research agenda.\nResearch Support – Collaborate with portfolio managers and senior researchers to translate investment ideas into well-documented, production-ready analytics and research findings.\nTechnology & Tools – Support the development and maintenance of analytical tools and codebases, primarily using Python and SQL, to enhance research workflows and investment processes.\nCommunication – Present research findings and analytical results clearly to diverse audiences, including Analysts, Portfolio Managers, and IT professionals, with varying levels of technical expertise.\n\nWho you are\n\nYou can demonstrate experience in Python (required) and SQL (preferred), including strong knowledge of machine learning libraries (e.g., scikit-learn, PyTorch, or TensorFlow). It's an asset if you have familiarity with quantitative research tools and financial data platforms.\nYou have a degree in a STEM field (Computer Science/Engineering, Physics, Mathematics, Statistics, or a related discipline). A graduate degree (Master's or PhD) is preferred.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1650,
        "completion_tokens": 385
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T20:59:02-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:clario-ai-engineer:google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite": {
      "input_hash": "115262686426bf22b62e85f07c4db64f2b0232ce4a9874b8721ee447a9bfed3f",
      "output": "What You'll Be Doing\n\n    Design, develop, and maintain AI-powered applications with a strong focus on Agentic AI, AI Agents, and LLM-enabled workflows\n    Build software services, APIs, and orchestration layers that connect AI models and tools into scalable production solutions\n    Contribute to the design, training, fine-tuning, evaluation, and deployment of AI models, including large language models and supporting ML components\n    Develop and optimize data pipelines for model training, retrieval, evaluation, and monitoring\n    Implement testing strategies, benchmarks, and quality controls to ensure AI systems are reliable, accurate, secure, and performant\n    Collaborate with AI engineers, software developers, scientists, and product managers to translate business requirements into technical solutions\n    Participate in the full software development lifecycle: design, implementation, testing, deployment, and monitoring in cloud environments (AWS preferred)\n    Apply engineering best practices for code quality, documentation, maintainability, and operational excellence\n    Support experimentation with new AI techniques, frameworks, and tooling, and help mature promising ideas into production capabilities\n    Stay up to date with advancements in generative AI, agentic systems, multi-modal AI, and cloud engineering\n\nWhat We're Looking For\n\n    Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or a related field (Master's a plus)\n    3+ years of experience in software engineering, AI engineering, machine learning, or a related technical field\n    Strong proficiency in Python and experience with AI/ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow\n    Experience building AI-enabled software applications and integrating machine learning or LLM capabilities into backend systems\n    Hands-on experience or strong interest in Agentic AI, AI Agents, tool-use workflows, or multi-step orchestration patterns\n    Familiarity with model training, fine-tuning, evaluation, prompt and workflow design, or model-serving concepts\n    Understanding of cloud-based architectures\n    Strong problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills\n    Commitment to code quality, security, scalability, and performance\n    Eagerness to learn, adapt, and stay current with emerging AI technologies and engineering practices",
