    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:kinaxis-data-analytics-coop-intern:inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash": {
      "input_hash": "b472a2ca016c1fade81cf1dd9ceba2e923ca59fb68a042ce6bb6e8e14cdc0c44",
      "output": "About The Team\n\nThe Data & Analytics team at Kinaxis drives transformation into a data-driven organization. By designing and governing scalable, modern data ecosystems, we ensure reliable, high-quality, and accessible data that empowers decision-making across the company. Our expertise spans data integration, engineering, governance, business intelligence, and cloud cost optimization.\n\nAs a Data & Analytics Intern/Co-op Student, you will have the opportunity to gain hands-on experience and develop skills in data integration, engineering, modeling, business intelligence, and observability. Working alongside experienced team members, you will help transform legacy systems into a cloud-native, modern data stack and create innovative data products that drive Kinaxis' decision-making. By contributing to the innovation of Kinaxis' data ecosystem, you will gain practical experience while playing a part in the company's growth and success.\n\nTerm Duration\n\nThis is a full-time, 8 month position, starting September, 2026.\n\nCo-op or Intern\n\nThis position is open to co-ops and interns. To be eligible for a Co-op or Intern position at Kinaxis, you must either be currently enrolled in full-time education or, if you are a recent/upcoming graduate, your graduation date must be within 12 months of the placement end date.\n\nCanadian Citizenship or Permanent Residency is required to obtain CGRP Security Clearance, a requirement of the role.\n\nWhat You Will Do\n\nModernization & Development\n\n     Assist in modernizing data systems with cloud-based tools. \n     Learn and apply modern data engineering practices and tools under guidance. \n     Develop basic data pipelines and integrations. \n     Participate in data validation, cleansing, and error-handling mechanisms to maintain data quality. \n     Stay updated on the latest technology trends relevant to your role. \n\nCollaboration & Solution Design\n\n     Work with team members to gather requirements and support small-scale data-driven solutions. \n     Contribute to team planning and the execution of data projects. \n     Troubleshoot issues while focusing on learning and skill development. \n     Work in an agile environment to deliver tasks collaboratively. \n\nInsights & Enablement\n\n     Create simple data models and dashboards to provide actionable insights to stakeholders. \n     Build and maintain visually appealing BI reports/dashboards. \n\nStorytelling & Influence\n\n     Learn to deliver compelling presentations to engage and inform stakeholders. \n\nWhat We Are Looking For\n\n     Currently enrolled in a Bachelor's degree program in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related fields. \n     Exposure to SQL, Python, or data pipeline tools (e.g., Airflow, dbt) through coursework or previous projects. \n     Exposure to BI tools such as PowerBI and/or Looker is a plus \n     Basic understanding of software engineering principles, including CI/CD pipelines, version control (Git), and RESTful APIs. \n     Basic knowledge of database concepts and different types of data models. \n     Interest in infrastructure-as-code (Terraform) and/or configuration-as-code (Ansible) is a plus. \n     A passion for learning and solving technical challenges. \n     Must be a Canadian Citizen or a Permanent Resident due to CGRP security requirements",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1280,
        "completion_tokens": 1478
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
