    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:clio-ml-engineer:openai/gpt-5.4-nano": {
      "input_hash": "24498087307123962f69f6eb25c6dad8c446542388ec4ff42e6aeec568f6e531",
      "output": "About the job\n\nSummary:\n\nWe are currently seeking a Machine Learning Engineer to join our rapidly growing engineering team. This role is for someone who is passionate about building innovative solutions and being exposed to new challenges and technologies while making an impact.\n\nThis role is available to candidates across Canada (excluding Quebec). If you are local to one of our hubs (Burnaby, Calgary, or Toronto) you will be expected to be in office minimum twice per week on one of our Anchor Days.\n\nWhat your team does:\n\nWe at Clio have an amazing team that is on a mission to transform the legal experience for all, and our engineering team’s goal is to deliver an incredible experience to our customers. In the AI team in Clio, we use the latest technology in the space of NLP and GenAI to provide our customers with solutions to make their work more streamlined and efficient allowing them to have more time to focus on their clients’ needs.\n\nA day in the life might look like:\n\n    Develop advanced machine learning models using structured and unstructured data to improve Clio’s customer’s experience\n    Create LLMs based solutions to help Clio’s clients to save time and create efficiencies\n    Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product management, operations and data science to identify new ML-driven features for Clio customers\n    Work in an agile environment with our team of machine learning engineers, MLOps engineering and full stack developers across a variety of projects\n\nWhat you may have:\n\n    Hands-on experience in model development, particularly with traditional machine learning, NLP, and transformer-based models;\n    Proficiency in data manipulation, cleaning, and preprocessing for complex unstructured datasets;\n    Experience with agentic frameworks and workflows \n    Experience working with open-source LLM foundation models and APIs for commercial LLMs, such as ChatGPT or Gemini;\n    A proven ability to quickly learn new technologies and adapt to a dynamic, fast-paced environment with distributed teams and customers;\n    A portfolio of past projects showcasing your successes, challenges, and growth as a machine learning expert;\n    Exceptional communication skills and the ability to build trust with both internal teams and external customers;\n    A strong desire to continuously learn, challenge yourself, and refine your craft as a machine learning engineer.\n\nThis posting is for an existing vacancy.",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1005,
        "completion_tokens": 464
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T21:09:39-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:coca-cola-data-scientist:openai/gpt-5.4-nano": {
      "input_hash": "153868931b46d65bb26fbb9c3f18d2a861ab725078e5e5952a486b976b9eb676",
      "output": "Coke Canada Bottling is Canada’s Local Bottler. We’re Made Local.\n\nProudly independent, we are a Canadian, family-owned business. Coke Canada Bottling makes, distributes, merchandises, and sells the most-loved beverages Canadians enjoy. With over 6,000 diverse employees coast-to-coast, we operate in every province through 50+ sales and distribution centres, and five manufacturing facilities.\n\nCoke Canada supplies some of Canada’s favourite beverage brands, and we want to continue to be the leading beverage partner in Canada, creating a better future and delivering optimism by bringing sustainable value to our employees, customers, consumers, and communities.\n\nAdvancing a high-performing, collaborative and inclusive culture is at the core of our vision to be the World’s Greatest Bottler, Built by the Best People, and we’re looking for exceptional talent to help get us there.\n\nFor more information about Coke Canada Bottling and our products, visit cokecanada.com/our-product.\n\nRole Details\n\n    Work Location – Toronto\n    Hybrid Environment – This position currently offers a hybrid work schedule. Subject to change. The in-office requirement is a minimum of three days per week (Tuesday, Wednesday & Thursday), with the flexibility to work remotely on the remaining days.\n    Initial Posting Close Date – July 30, 2026\n\nAbout This Opportunity\n\nWe are recruiting for a Data Scientist to join our Data Science and Advanced Analytics team. This Advanced Analytics role is part of the broader Technology function and plays a key role in supporting high impact, data driven initiatives across the organization. The team partners with stakeholders in commercial strategy, sales execution, and operations to address complex business challenges through advanced analytics and machine learning.\n\nAs a Data Scientist, you will contribute to cross functional projects involving demand modeling, promotion and trade spend optimization, pricing and elasticity analysis, network and inventory optimization, and scenario modeling. You will work closely with business partners to translate exploratory analytical work into scalable, production ready solutions that enhance planning, strengthen decision making, and improve execution across the organization.\n\nThis is an exciting opportunity to leverage your experience in data science, advanced analytics, or applied machine learning to help solve meaningful business challenges and turn complex data into practical, scalable insights.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n    Contribute to analytics initiatives using statistical and machine learning techniques to solve business problems in demand forecasting, pricing, and product optimization.\n    Support the development and improvement of analytical models to understand demand drivers and price elasticity, ensuring insights are practical, reliable, and business-relevant.\n    Assist in building tools and analytical processes that improve trade spend effectiveness and promotional performance, enabling smarter commercial and sales decisions.\n    Support analytics initiatives that enhance operational planning and execution, applying data-driven insights as the function expands into operations-focused areas.\n    Create clear visualizations and collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate data insights into actionable recommendations for commercial, sales, and operations stakeholders.\n\nQualifications\n\n    Bachelor’s degree or a college diploma in a quantitative or technical field (e.g., Statistics, Mathematics, Data Science, Engineering); a Master’s degree is considered an asset.\n    3+ years of experience in data science, advanced analytics, or applied machine learning roles, with exposure to business-focused analytics.\n    Strong experience working with large, complex datasets and proficiency in SQL and Python.\n    Experience applying statistical modeling and machine learning techniques, such as regression-based models, tree-based models and optimization approaches.\n    Foundational understanding of demand forecasting, elasticity modeling, promotional analysis, or scenario modeling.\n    Familiarity with analytics development within Databricks and the Azure data ecosystem is considered an asset.\n    Strong proficiency in data visualization tools such as Power BI (preferred) or Tableau.\n    Ability to communicate analytical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n    Proactive mindset with the ability to work through ambiguity, take initiative, and suggest new analytical approaches or opportunities to improve business outcomes.\n\n#CBSAS\n#LI-KS1",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 1398,
        "completion_tokens": 795
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T21:09:46-0400"
    },
    "cb5385d50a40d64c8961b3b3be574d65af7897c66e5bf2b6b1e4d5779ddc22c1:dayforce-product-ai-intern:openai/gpt-5.4-nano": {
      "input_hash": "37770a9a1ef03c1c857404b657e9c233757406d3ff265cf926ed7e491bcc3214",
      "output": "Dayforce, a global leader in Human Capital Management (HCM) with headquarters in Toronto, Ontario, and Minneapolis, Minnesota, operates across North America, EMEA, and APJ regions. Our Cloud HCM platform, recognized for its unified database and continuous calculation engine, enhances efficiency, productivity, and compliance for global workforces. \n\nAs an Intern at Dayforce, you’ll gain real-world experience with meaningful responsibilities, access to development programs, and the chance to collaborate globally, bringing new ideas and optimizing processes across multiple business units. \n\nJob Title: Product & AI Intern\n\nLocation: Virtual\n\nDuration: Fall 2026 – 4 months (September 2026 – December 2026)\n\nAvailability: *Full-time availability of 37.5 – 40 hours weekly is required to be eligible for this opportunity.\n\nAbout The Opportunity\n\nWe are seeking a technical AI Product Intern to support our GenAI and AI Agent product initiatives. In this role, you will work directly with the AI product team to develop prototypes that spark future product innovation, as well as help improve model performance, evaluate multilingual model output quality. Furthermore, you will have the opportunity to help us evolve our product analytics capabilities in Pendo, and craft meaningful content in Confluence. This internship is ideal for a Computer Science or Engineering student with a passion for machine learning, AI, experimentation, and turning messy problems into working solutions.\n\nWhat You’ll Get To Do\n\n    Build working demos in live code to communicate product opportunities\n    Create annotated datasets to improve our LLM-based systems\n    Assist with hands-on evaluation of multilingual model output\n    Develop and refine product analytics in Pendo and analyze product usage data in Pendo and Databricks to generate insights that inform our roadmap\n    Craft and refine meaningful content and documentation (e.g. Confluence) for broad stakeholder communications\n    Support our teams’ development workflows and experimentation infrastructure\n\nSkills And Experience We Value\n\n    Proven experience with machine learning, preferably GenAI or LLM applications\n    Experience with programming languages: Python and SQL, etc.\n    Comfort with tools such as (or similar to): Databricks, Pendo, Visual Studio, etc.\n    Entrepreneurial mindset: works with minimal guidance and solves their own problems\n    Ability to translate ambiguous tasks into clear outputs\n    Strong communication skills and curiosity about how product and ML intersect\n\nWhat Would Really Make You Stand Out\n\n    Front-end experience (React, Streamlit, etc.) for prototyping\n    Familiarity with multilingual NLP or localization tools",
      "usage": {
        "prompt_tokens": 942,
        "completion_tokens": 516
      },
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-19T21:09:52-0400"
